<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 11 October, from 1138 to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1138">1138 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">888 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A great earthquake strikes Aleppo and northern Syria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake struck <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> a day after a smaller shock, causing damage and chaos across the area. The toll of 230,000 later reported by Ibn Taghribirdi probably conflated it with other earthquakes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1142 CE <span class="tih-ago">884 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Shaoxing between Jin and Song is ratified</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-shaoxing">Treaty of Shaoxing</a>, signed in 1141, was formally ratified when a Jin envoy visited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> court. The Southern Song gave up its claims north of the Huai, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a>, and agreed to a yearly tribute to the Jin.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jin-song-wars">Jin–Song wars</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Leo X names Henry VIII 'Defender of the Faith'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pope Leo X granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> the title Fidei Defensor for his treatise attacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a>. Henry later broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, yet British monarchs still use the title, abbreviated 'F.D.' on coins.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1531">1531 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">495 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Catholic cantons defeat Zürich at the Battle of Kappel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Kappel am <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albi">Albis</a>, the Catholic cantons of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> defeated Protestant Zürich, and the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huldrych-zwingli">Huldrych Zwingli</a>, who accompanied the Zürich army as chaplain, was killed. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-peace-of-kappel">Second Peace of Kappel</a> halted the spread of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in the Confederacy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kappel">Battle of Kappel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A British force defeats Benedict Arnold's fleet at Valcour Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-champlain">Lake Champlain</a>, a British force under General Guy Carleton captured or destroyed most of the American fleet commanded by Benedict Arnold. The American defence of the lake nonetheless stalled British plans to reach the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-river">Hudson River</a> valley.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-champlain">Lake Champlain</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1899">1899 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">127 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Second Boer War begins in South Africa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">War broke out when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> let a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> ultimatum expire. In the three-year conflict that followed, British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a> saw the deaths of about 26,000 Boer women and children and many thousands of black Africans.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt receives Einstein's warning about atomic bombs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The economist Alexander Sachs delivered to Franklin Roosevelt a letter signed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-einstein">Albert Einstein</a>, warning that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> might build a uranium bomb. Roosevelt set up an advisory committee that led eventually to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan-project">Manhattan Project</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope John XXIII opens the Second Vatican Council</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">More than 2,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> gathered in St Peter's Basilica for the opening of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-vatican-council">Second Vatican Council</a>. Over three years it introduced vernacular liturgy, embraced ecumenism and affirmed religious freedom.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 11 October <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arthur-phillip"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arthur-phillip.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Arthur Phillip</span><span class="tp">1738–1814</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hans-kelsen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hans-kelsen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hans Kelsen</span><span class="tp">1881–1973</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 11 October <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bruno-the-great"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bruno-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bruno the Great</span><span class="tp">925–965</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-boniface-viii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-boniface-viii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Boniface VIII</span><span class="tp">c. 1230–1303</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-iv-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-iv-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis IV, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1282–1347</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jan-zizka"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jan-zizka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jan Žižka</span><span class="tp">c. 1360–1424</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/huldrych-zwingli"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/huldrych-zwingli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Huldrych Zwingli</span><span class="tp">1484–1531</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ehrenfried-walther-von-tschirnhaus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ehrenfried-walther-von-tschirnhaus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ehrenfried Walther von Tschirnhaus</span><span class="tp">1651–1708</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
